Having only to choose, remarked Dean dryly.
What is the use of liking a lady who wont like me?
If Dean Priest were acynic he showed no cynicism to Emily.
Oh, Mother, she said, what did you think of when you were alittle girl here=
 like me?
When Emily liftedthe lid a faint spicy odour floated out.
Cousin Jimmy has got Jimmy Joe Belle to help with the harvest.
She loved him for the world he opened toher view. He grasped her arms and p=
ulled her up beside himinto safety. She felt quite asrelieved then as if sh=
e had really said it. Aunt Elizabeth, snuffing the candles, glanced sharply=
 over herglasses.
Tell her that, said Emily coolly, with some of the Murrayshrewdness coming =
uppermost in her.
I believe I will, said Teddy, much impressed. He was not handsome but she l=
iked that lean, clever faceof his with its magnetic green eyes.
Are you never lonesome with only those twoold survivals? I wish she wouldnt=
 clapper-claw Perry so much.
But shefelt very badly when she turned to Dean. Emily, full of pluck, helpe=
d him bydigging her toes into the crumbling bank.
What squabble around a ballot-box will ever be that?
You make me believe in fairies, whether I will or no, he toldher, and that =
means youth.
When she wrote to her father a fewdays later she began the letter, Dear Fat=
her and Mother.
She is going to be married andIlse says that when her father heard it he sa=
id God help the man.
One burned with a steady upright flame likea faithful soul. Oh, Father dear=
 and Mother, we are going to have a new teacher. Cousin Jimmy says that is =
the wayluck always comes, and it is no use to look for it.
It seems so funny to think of ateacher having a wife and whiskers.
Do you always get what you go after, even withdeath slipping a thin wedge b=
etween?
I am writing a murder story now and I am trying to feel how a manwould feel=
 who was a murderer.
Because you see your life belongs to me henceforth. He was not handsome but=
 she liked that lean, clever faceof his with its magnetic green eyes.
Never before had shesensed Mrs Kents dislike for her so keenly as that nigh=
t.
I seem tosee myself visiting her very often henceforth. No, she said, its o=
nly my eyelashes and smile that are likeMothers.
Emily HAD grown, taller and older, insoul, if not in body.
But I cant believe in fairies myself, protested Emilysorrowfully.
She doesnt make me wearsunbonnets and she lets me go barefooted in the fore=
noons. Emily HAD grown, taller and older, insoul, if not in body.
One of them,hanging over the head of the bed, represented two guardian ange=
ls.
If a girl named Mary marries a man named Leon she will alwaysbe called Mary=
 Leon after that.
She doesnt mean that as a compliment, whatever you in yourinnocence believe=
 it to be.=20
